WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.920
An Australian Tesla driver has clocked 600,000 miles on his model s, with only one battery change. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 617. A zoog's robotaxi struck a Nissan in Las Vegas. The incident was captured on video by a local account and shared publicly. No injuries were reported in the initial account. The post received 18.9,000 views according to Tesla Roddy. The Tesla Roddy founder stated a starship

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:35.440
launch is something he needs to see in his lifetime. He described it as wildly emotional

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:41.580
to witness. Elon Musk replied with a reference to the mandate of heaven. The post received

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:49.220
17,400 views. Elon Musk said in a China media group interview that Neuralink aims to bridge

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:56.060
the gap between humans and AI. Humans communicate at roughly 100 bits per second, while computers

00:00:56.060 --> 00:01:01.740
appears exchanged trillions. Musk argued boosting human bandwidth may be essential for alignment.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:06.860
The post received 881 views according to TSLA Ming.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:12.880
Matthias Tiala discovered a charge port heater option in the service menu. The feature

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:19.720
heats the recess charge port to prevent frost issues. The video has been viewed over 372,000

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:24.920
times according to motor one. Tiala lives in Ohio and believes the feature will come

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.420
in handy during winter months.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:30.520
Viewers reported checking their own vehicles after seeing the video.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.960
Elon Musk praised President Xi for visible progress in China during his tenure.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:41.180
He credited Chinese manufacturing ability for the success of Gigafactory Shanghai.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:47.260
Musk noted that progress in China is visible year-to-year through new buildings and infrastructure.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:53.800
Ross Gerber asked why Starlink runs television ads, but Tesla does not when gasoline prices

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:59.820
are elevated. He suggested the company could sell more vehicles with advertising. The national

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:07.000
average for regular gasoline reached $4.44 per gallon as of September 21 according to Benzinga.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:12.800
Goldman Sachs lowered its third-quarter delivery estimate to 435,000 vehicles.

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:18.640
Weekly Optimus production reached several hundred units last month. The goal is a continuous

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:25.400
automated line producing over 1,000 robots a week by year end. Each hand contains more than 100

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:32.220
screws that still require human assembly according to Finance.bigo. Touch sensors in the hands have

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:38.680
shown reliability issues. Tesla plans to integrate a glove-like sensor layer in a future model next year.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:46.040
Nigel Raynard reached 600,000 miles after eight years of ownership. He upgraded to a 90-kilowatt

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:54.720
hour pack under warranty at 666,000 km. The car has achieved 186 watt-hours per km efficiency

00:02:54.720 --> 00:03:02.860
since the replacement. Raynard obtains between 50,000 and 75,000 km per tire set. Tesla

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:08.360
ended its semi-event with a roadster teaser showing a new front light bar. The video suggests

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:14.820
changes from the original 2017 design according to Tesla Roddy. Tesla scheduled an October

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:16.400
over one roadster unveiling.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.620
The event follows years of delays

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.180
on the high-performance vehicle

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:21.520
according to Yahoo Finance.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.640
Tesla increased its share of the US electric vehicle market

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.460
even as overall sales declined.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.980
The company is working to maintain margins amid the shift.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.920
The article examines whether Tesla can protect

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:36.500
automotive margins according to Yahoo Finance.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:40.320
Tesla opened a new semi-production facility in Nevada.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.360
Output is scaling toward an annual capacity

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.500
of 50,000 trucks according to Intellectia AI.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:51.200
A lawsuit claims a Tesla vehicle exploded inside a Florida garage.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.600
The incident destroyed the home and killed the family dog.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:59.700
The case is moving forward in court according to independent.co.uk.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.420
The European Union postponed a vote on Tesla full self-driving supervised until at least

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:06.000
December.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:11.220
The Technical Committee on Motor Vehicles Agenda lists only continuation of discussions.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:17.200
actions. The delay affects the plan October 6 review according to Tesslerotti. The technical

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:22.360
committee on motor vehicles will not vote on full self-driving supervised before December.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:29.020
The agenda item was reduced to 25 minutes of continued discussion. Regulators in the Netherlands

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:35.100
had raised prior concerns according to Electric. Some Tesla employees have expressed reluctance

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:40.520
to train optimist robots that could eventually replace human roles. The resistance centers

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:44.620
on job security concerns during the humanoid rollout according to R's

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:49.760
Technica. Elon Musk stated at least one billion humanoid robots could be

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:55.380
deployed within 10 years. He listed eldercare, child supervision, and personalized

00:04:55.380 --> 00:05:01.100
tutoring as example uses according to ABAB news. Ross Gerber publicly questioned

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:05.760
why Tesla is not running television ads for its electric vehicles while gasoline

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:11.600
prices climb. He noted Starlink advertisements appear regularly, and suggested the lack

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:17.020
of promotion misses an opportunity. The human brain processes language and sensory input

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:23.320
at roughly 100 bits per second, while modern AI systems move data at trillions of bits per second.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:29.300
That gap is not a temporary inconvenience. It is a structural mismatch that grows with every

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:35.460
improvement in model scale and inference speed. Neuralinx approach treats the disparity as an engineering

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:40.700
problem rather than a philosophical one. By increasing the bandwidth of the neural interface,

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:46.100
the system aims to let humans exchange information at rates closer to those of the machines they

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:51.800
interact with. Early targets focus on restoring function for people with neurological conditions,

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:57.260
yet the same hardware path could eventually support higher throughput communication for healthy users.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:04.040
If the bandwidth increase materializes, the practical effect would be faster iteration between human intent

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:08.540
and machine output. Training loops for both full self-driving and

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:12.820
optimist would shorten, because human feedback could arrive at machine native

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:17.540
speeds. The cost curve for that feedback would drop from hours of annotation

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:22.820
time to seconds of direct neural input, altering the economics of scaling both

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:29.220
autonomy and robotics programs. Before we go, an October 1 Roadster unveiling is

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:32.980
scheduled next week. And that's a wrap on today's Tesla news.

